WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.980
This story is a simple illustration of the three
.Minami sisters and the ordinary life they lead.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.010
Please don't expect too much from it.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:19.580
Also, please sit at least three meters from the television in a well-lit room when watching.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.080
You moron.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.840
Afternoon.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.380
Hello, Makoto.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.510
Haruka-san and Chiaki aren't home yet?

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.280
They're out shopping today.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.740
I'll change in the next room.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.030
Hello, Mako-chan.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:49.770
What brings you here?

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.280
I brought another cookbook.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.900
Haruka said she wanted to read it.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:05.480
Kana.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.080
I want to put an end to this charade.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:09.000
Why the sudden change?

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:09.910
Fifty-five.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:11.090
Don't you think it's weird?!

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:14.090
I mean, having to dress up as
.a girl just to visit a classmate.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.970
But there's no way you could
get in here as Makoto.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.020
I know that.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:24.370
I know Chiaki wouldn't
.invite me here as Makoto.

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:26.060
But I can't take it anymore.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.730
My inner man is telling me
that this is all wrong.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.220
I think you'll be fine.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.310
No I won't!

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.950
Sooner or later, she'll figure out who I am!

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:38.350
I mean, I have this uncontrollable wild side

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:40.490
and was born with these rugged good looks!

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:42.930
I think you'll be fine.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:44.860
You could at least pretend to care, Kana!

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:47.260
I mean, <i>you're</i> the one who put me up to this!

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:50.000
It's already out of my hands.

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:56.300
How much longer do I have to lie to Haruka-san and Chiaki?

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:00.930
I guess you're right.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.190
We're home!

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.190
Welcome home!

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:08.840
Oh, Mako-chan.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:09.690
Welcome.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.690
I brought the cookbook
.we talked about before.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.320
Oh, thank you.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.660
Would you like to help make
something while you're here?

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:18.820
Yes!

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:21.460
Hey, Chiaki.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:22.490
What?

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.370
Mako-chan's pretty cute, right?

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:25.200
Yeah.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.620
She's very ladylike.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.500
You should learn from her example.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:28.900
Yeah, I should learn to be more like her.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:31.150
So, Mako-chan, what do you want to cook?

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.580
Let's try this "beef stroganoff" thing.
Yeah, I should learn to be more like her.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:34.000
Let's try this "beef stroganoff" thing.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:11.910
What?!

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:13.310
Call the fire department!

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.040
Hurry!

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.200
The fire department...

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.110
What was their number?

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.200
Touma!

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.320
Touma, are you okay?

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:19.400
Just kidding.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.320
It was a joke.

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:22.770
Run, Touma!

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:23.650
Get out of here!

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.950
I said it was a joke!

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:30.410
Oh, so today's April Fools' Day.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:32.500
April Fools'?

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:35.540
Who celebrates that? We sure don't.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.460
There are plenty of stories regarding the origin of April Fools' Day.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.800
The most likely one
..originates from France...

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:45.130
That was out of line, even
.for an April Fools' joke.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.720
How should we punish her?

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:50.350
She's going without
.dinner tonight for sure.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:53.350
Natsuki, that's a bit harsh.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:53.370
Touma's a girl.
Natsuki, that's a bit harsh.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:54.520
Touma's a girl.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.560
Stay out of this, Haruo.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:59.280
I think that punishment is too lenient.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:00.820
Even for a girl.

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:02.990
Stay out of this, Akira.

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:04.880
He's already made up his mind!

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:07.170
But I'm the oldest one here.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.360
Stay out of this, Haruo.

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:13.000
So, since I can't eat at home,

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.200
I was wondering if
.I could eat here instead.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.040
I see.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.910
Today's April Fools'.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:20.420
That's right. I didn't do anything wrong.

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:23.920
I kinda wanna play a prank of my own.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:27.390
Coming.

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:30.140
Hello?

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:33.930
Oh, Akira.

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:35.650
Yeah.

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:36.850
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:38.480
I see.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.280
So Touma went too far with one of her lies

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:43.730
and now you want me, liar
..extraordinaire, to teach her a lesson?

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:45.550
Who're you calling a liar?

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:46.860
That's rude, you know.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.080
Hey, Minami.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.040
Is Touma there?

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:54.600
Oh, Fujioka.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.910
Yeah, she's here.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.500
But what kind of prank should I pull?

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:04.550
Touma, we want to extend soccer practice a bit starting next week. Is that okay?

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.800
Huh? Aren't we doing enough already?

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.440
Don't be a wimp!

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:13.540
If we don't step things up now, you'll have
.a hard time adjusting in middle school.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:15.680
But still...

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.810
Enough whining!

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.310
Real men don't do that.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:20.820
But...

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:22.320
But I'm a girl.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:25.480
Real men...

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:28.700
Fujioka.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:31.310
Soccer practice is all well and good,

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:33.780
but you shouldn't make
.Touma work too hard.

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:35.160
She may not look it,

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.950
but she's a girl, you know.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:42.250
All right? Go easy on her.

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:48.090
K-Kana! Why did you tell him that?!

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.110
Calm down, Touma.

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:52.400
That was just an April Fools' joke.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:53.220
A joke?

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:58.110
The best lies are the ones
.that mix fact with fiction.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:06:59.930
But that was entirely fact!

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:02.980
Yes. A lie that's all fact and no fiction.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:07.110
I bet Fujioka totally bought it.

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.780
That's not a good thing!

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:16.660
We were only able to talk about soccer so much because he thought I was a boy.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:18.580
Touma!

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:23.170
Touma.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:26.420
This is so awkward.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:27.800
I see.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.110
So Touma's a girl.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:31.630
That explains why she's so cute.

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:39.230
Thanks for having me!

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:44.310
Just so you know, Touma is...

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.230
No, I get it.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.980
It's April Fools' Day today, after all.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:50.330
<b>Minami</b>

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:51.310
Kana-san.
<b>Minami</b>

00:07:51.310 --> 00:07:54.320
I know I asked you to
.teach Touma a lesson,
<b>Minami</b>

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:57.580
but she's been wrapped up in bed ever since she came home.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.500
What did you do?

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:02.080
Did I go too far?

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:03.510
Touma.

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:05.710
If you apologize now,
I'll make you dinner.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:08.260
It's fine.

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:09.800
I'm not hungry.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.800
Chiaki, Mako-chan is actually a boy.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.480
Hey!

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:16.840
You can come up with a better April Fools' joke than that.

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:18.810
You're being mean to Mako-chan. Isn't she?

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:20.960
Yeah...

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:26.150
All right, we'll decide who's right with a sumo wrestling match!

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:28.270
What? How come?

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:30.570
Real men duke it out by sumo wrestling!

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:36.680
That pork stroganoff that Mako-chan and
.Haruka-neesama made was pretty good, though.

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:38.080
Pork? Not beef?

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.800
We didn't have any beef.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:42.130
You and Mako-chan seem pretty close.

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:44.130
Yeah, she's one of my best friends.

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:45.460
So what do you think of Makoto-kun?

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:47.420
I don't hate him.

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:49.380
R-Really?

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:51.200
I don't hate him.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:53.420
I just hate how he's not manly at all.

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:55.380
So you <i>do</i> hate him.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:57.390
Did someone call for me?

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:58.970
I feel like someone here wanted to see me.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.130
No one did.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:03.350
Who'd want to see a wimp like you?

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:04.310
Wh-What?!

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:07.510
We were asking what Chiaki thought of you.

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:09.570
Did she say I was a nice guy,
bursting with manliness?

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:11.610
She said you weren't manly at all.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:13.460
S-She did?

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:16.240
But I've been trying so hard...

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:19.040
You do act like a man sometimes, though.

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:19.660
Right?

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.730
Yeah.

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:23.290
Like that one time we
.went over to Chiaki's house.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.530
What's wrong, Haruka?

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:28.580
Haruka-neesama, what happened?

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.340
A wasp flew in through the window!

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:36.970
I'll take care of it, Haruka-san!

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:43.250
Oh, that's right. You were really brave back there, Makoto-ku—

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:53.650
I, uh... I mean Mako-chan, not Makoto-kun.

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:55.900
Oh, that's right.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:58.060
Sorry, I got them confused.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:01.320
Their names just sound so similar.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:05.700
Hey, Uchida.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:10.210
Do you think Yoshino's realized that
Mako-chan and I are the same person?

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:12.150
I don't know.

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:13.840
I really don't know, Mako-chan.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.560
I'm Makoto right now, though.

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:17.630
I'm sorry.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:24.180
Kana. I need to talk to you.

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:29.020
I know that I might not be all that manly,

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:34.020
but what little masculinity I have is begging me to stop this.

00:10:36.470 --> 00:10:38.600
I'm done being Mako-chan.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:41.950
So I'm giving back this hairpin.
I don't need it anymore.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:44.640
Okay.

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:47.680
If that's what you want, it's fine.

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:48.710
Fifty-six.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:52.060
That sounds kind of familiar.

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:53.630
What do you mean, "fifty-six"?

00:10:57.130 --> 00:11:00.010
That's the number of times you've said you're done being Mako-chan.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:02.320
This time's for real!

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:04.810
The laundry's done.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:10.600
It's time to show me how serious you are.

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:11.940
You bet!

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:14.520
Um, Haruka-san.

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:15.690
Huh?

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:19.530
Oh, you're not wearing your
hairpin today, Mako-chan?

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:21.530
Well, that's...

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.370
It looked really cute on you.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.820
Haruka-san said it looked cute...

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:30.900
It looked cute...

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:36.040
Did you lose it?

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:37.460
Yeah, I did.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:38.830
I see.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:41.180
I'll be right back, okay?

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:47.840
Don't you have something to say to me?

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:50.100
Why? It always turns out this way.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:51.600
Here.

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:52.730
You can have this.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:55.730
But I...

00:11:56.110 --> 00:12:00.490
You've been a good friend to Chiaki, so just think of it as my way of saying thanks.

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:03.000
Chiaki's really taken a liking to you,

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:04.410
so I hope you two stay good friends.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:06.410
Haruka-san!

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:09.410
Haruka-neesama, I bought the milk.

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:11.880
Thanks, Chiaki.

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:15.030
All right, time to get ready for dinner.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:17.880
A spade-shaped hairpin, huh?

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.880
They say the spade symbol
.is derived from a sword.

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:22.050
A sword?

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.510
It suits you, Mako-chan.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:27.140
You can be manly when we need you to be.

00:12:27.530 --> 00:12:28.930
It suits me?

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:30.640
Manly?

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:34.550
I see. Haruka-san has entrusted me with this sword,

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:37.650
along with the duty of staying
.forever faithful to Chiaki.

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:40.150
I'm like a knight!

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:44.030
And if I can't fulfill my duty
..as a knight as Makoto...

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:47.910
I am Mako-chan once more!

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.880
All right, Chiaki! Let's have some fun!

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:51.910
It's pretty late. Shouldn't
you start heading home?

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:53.220
You're right.

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:54.920
See you next time!

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:15.140
Thanks for the food.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:15.930
<b>Minami</b>

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:17.150
I'm off.
<b>Minami</b>

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:18.730
Touma.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:20.250
Clean up after yourself.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:22.570
Do it.

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.030
Fine.

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:31.760
Thanks for the food.

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:33.370
Hey, Natsuki.

00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:35.260
Thanks for the food.

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:36.250
What is it, Brother?

00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:38.950
This is something that's been
.bothering me for a while.

00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:41.050
But I have no choice but
.to accept it as the truth.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.250
What is it?

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:44.760
Touma isn't very ladylike.

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:47.510
No, she just doesn't clean up after herself.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:51.910
A girl her age should not
only clean up after herself,

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:52.820
but cook for her beloved brothers as well.

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:54.400
I'm off!
but cook for her beloved brothers as well.

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:54.890
but cook for her beloved brothers as well.

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:58.230
True, the girls at the other
.Minami residence <i>do</i> cook.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:00.930
Thanks for the food.

00:14:00.930 --> 00:14:03.620
You guys should clean
.up after yourselves too.

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:05.030
You always leave your
.plates and stuff behind.

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:07.480
We're having an important
.discussion right now.

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:09.470
Stay out of this, Akira.

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:10.690
Oh, look at the time.

00:14:10.690 --> 00:14:11.870
We should get going.

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:12.430
Yeah.

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:15.280
We should talk to her about this.

00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:16.210
I'll talk to her.

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:18.510
Wait. It'd be better if I did.

00:14:18.510 --> 00:14:18.960
No, I will.
Wait. It'd be better if I did.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:19.820
No, I will.

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:21.040
This is important. I'll do it.

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:21.710
Stay out of this, Brother!

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:22.410
And in the end, I'm stuck cleaning up.
Stay out of this, Brother!

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:23.800
And in the end, I'm stuck cleaning up.

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:26.720
Hey, what does it mean to be "ladylike"?

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:28.770
Why do you ask?

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:32.220
My brothers have been saying
.that I'm not ladylike enough.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:37.430
So I figured I should learn all I could
.about it from someone I knew who was.

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:40.020
Oh, but I don't know what to tell you.

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:42.310
Why don't you ask me?

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:45.400
I'm sure there's someone better
.than me who you could ask.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:46.780
Like who?

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:48.150
What about me?

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:53.530
Maybe we should ask a guy what
.they think it means to be ladylike.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:54.790
Makoto-kun.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:59.550
What do you think it
means to be ladylike?

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:00.370
Wh-What do you mean?

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:03.340
Do I look like someone who'd know?

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:08.170
We just wanted to get a guy's opinion.

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:09.750
Oh, I see.

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:13.320
I guess I <i>am</i> a man among men, after all.

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:17.770
But I don't really know.

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.330
Maybe you should ask Chiaki.

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:20.610
What about me?

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:25.520
<b>Femininity</b>

00:15:25.850 --> 00:15:27.470
It's all too easy for "femininity"

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:31.630
<b>Femininity
to become "effeminacy" if you don't know when to stop.</b>

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:32.610
<b>Femininity</b>

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:32.620
That's really nice.
<b>Femininity</b>

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:34.750
That's really nice.

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:36.120
Way to go.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:38.120
It's best to just be yourself.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.500
But that hasn't worked.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:44.310
Maybe there's some part of you
.that you don't know about, though.

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:45.840
Something ladylike.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.670
Do you have any feminine hobbies?

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:49.800
I don't think so.

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:51.750
I can't think of any.

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:53.000
Oh, right,

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:55.350
you have this strange air
.of femininity to you, Chiaki.

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:57.350
A strange air?

00:15:57.350 --> 00:16:00.350
I don't know why, seeing as how
.everything you do and say is so violent.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:00.840
Hey!

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:02.570
But what makes you seem so feminine?

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:04.850
Does Chiaki seem feminine right now?

00:16:05.510 --> 00:16:06.860
Not really.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:07.480
Hey!

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:11.070
But when she's home, she really does.

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:12.290
I got it!

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:14.950
When she holds her stuffed toy,
that's when it happens.

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:18.240
So it's Fujioka?!

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:20.950
<i>Fujioka</i> is what makes me feminine?!

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:23.650
Well, stuffed toys <i>are</i> a very feminine hobby.

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:25.110
Stuffed toys...

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:26.860
They're easy enough to make,

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:28.550
but it's a lot harder to
.bring myself to hold them.

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:29.500
You can make them?

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:33.680
I mean, you just cut the cloth, stuff it with cotton, and sew it up, right?

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:35.510
I'm pretty good at craft work like that.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:37.770
So you can sew?

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:39.330
That's very ladylike.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:40.600
Yeah.

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:42.770
Sewing and craft work are different?

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:44.000
<b>Minami</b>

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:44.840
Touma.
<b>Minami</b>

00:16:44.840 --> 00:16:45.770
Are you there?
<b>Minami</b>

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:45.780
<b>Minami</b>

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:48.340
If so, you should clean up the bath—

00:16:58.670 --> 00:17:00.010
This cloth...

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:01.700
And this cotton...

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:04.210
Who did this to our cushion?!

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:09.240
Please, Haruka-neesama.

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:10.590
Okay, but...

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:12.610
Like this?

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:13.920
Oh!

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:18.100
Oh, you made this, Touma?

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:20.040
It's really good.

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:20.910
I guess.

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:22.510
I'm pretty good at craft work.

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:24.350
It looks just like Fujioka.

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:30.220
My brothers say it's really comfy to put their heads on when they lie down.

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:31.820
Sounds more like a pillow.

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:36.320
But I bet if we switched these two, Chiaki wouldn't even notice.

00:17:36.690 --> 00:17:38.330
No way.

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:40.860
The material and color aren't even close.

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:41.580
Huh?

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:44.830
There's something off about Kana today.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:46.080
Touma.

00:17:46.470 --> 00:17:49.580
Here are some materials
.you might be able to use.

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:51.800
They're old clothes from around the house.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:54.280
Can I really have these?

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:55.170
Sure.

00:17:55.170 --> 00:18:00.050
So, did you bring the stuffed
toy you said you'd made?

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:06.060
I can't really show you right now... or maybe I already have.

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:07.480
What do you mean?

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:08.940
Is this a riddle?

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:11.060
Huh?!

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:12.140
Huh?

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:14.070
What? What happened?

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:17.220
Something... is different!

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:19.730
That's right! Something <i>is</i> different!

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:20.950
What do you mean?

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:22.170
You! Kana!

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:23.580
You did something to him!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.420
I did something, did I?

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:27.870
And just what would
that "something" be?

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:30.710
Chiaki...

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:33.710
Take a good look around you
.with those half-closed eyes.

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:38.510
The world that you see is always changing.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:40.640
What was that for?!

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:42.730
You were being cheeky.

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:44.640
Is that any way to treat your own sister?

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:49.530
If you really are my sister,
start acting like one.

00:18:49.530 --> 00:18:51.430
Oh! I know what it is!

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:54.170
What did you figure out?

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:56.260
Kana! You're in low spirits today!

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:57.550
M-Me?

00:18:57.550 --> 00:18:59.440
What do you mean?

00:18:59.440 --> 00:19:02.410
I'd say I'm in perfectly
.normal spirits today.

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:06.570
That's weird. I could've sworn that was it.

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:08.120
Is it just me?

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:10.170
Something's off.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:14.840
Take a good look at me. What else is low?

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:16.110
Your blood pressure?

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:18.920
No, that rises every time you guess wrong.

00:19:19.310 --> 00:19:21.310
Are your test scores still low?

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:22.930
Blood pressure going up!

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:24.770
You're lower on the totem
pole than your sisters?

00:19:24.770 --> 00:19:26.510
Blood pressure going up!

00:19:26.510 --> 00:19:28.400
Oh! It must be your femininity that's low!

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:30.350
Blood pressure going through the roof!

00:19:31.490 --> 00:19:33.060
I see, Touma.

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:35.770
You've already noticed what's different about me, but you're not saying it!

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:38.280
Then I'm not going to tell you the answer!

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:42.170
That just makes me even more curious.

00:19:42.170 --> 00:19:44.370
Something's off about Kana, right?

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:46.790
Even if there were, what
do you want me to say?

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:51.150
The world that you see is always changing.

00:19:51.150 --> 00:19:53.790
What's the point in trying to resist?

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:55.790
Accept change!

00:19:56.180 --> 00:19:58.770
You've accepted that stuffed toy?

00:19:58.770 --> 00:19:59.970
Fine. I get it.

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:01.470
I won't bother you any longer.

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:03.570
I'll be going home.

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:04.820
Thanks for the clothes.

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:05.850
Sure.

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:07.470
Wait, Touma!

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:13.520
I just tied my hair a little lower today.

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:18.280
You're right!

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:35.610
Who're you?!

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:37.790
I'm home.

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:41.050
Wow, you made this, Touma?

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:43.420
I'm pretty good at craft work.

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:44.800
Craft work?

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:49.080
I hear it's really comfy to put
.your head on when you lie down.

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:51.000
Well, it <i>was</i> made from a cushion, after all.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.060
A cushion?

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:54.640
I bet you could make something great from curtains too.

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:57.160
Yeah, I could probably make some clothes.

00:20:57.960 --> 00:20:58.730
Really?

00:20:58.730 --> 00:20:58.740
They're easier to make than stuffed toys.
Really?

00:20:58.740 --> 00:21:01.040
They're easier to make than stuffed toys.

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:02.610
You don't need to stuff
.cotton into them, for one.

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:07.110
Hey, could you make this for me?

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:08.260
And this for me?

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:09.950
S-Sure, if you like...

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:12.330
Touma, would you like
to stay for dinner?

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:13.170
Yeah!

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:14.170
I see.

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:16.330
Anyway, dinner aside,

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:17.960
I quite like <i>these</i> kinds of clothes.

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:18.950
Sure.

00:21:18.950 --> 00:21:22.130
Dinner aside, I'll make them for you.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:22.820
Perfect.

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:24.960
Eat well tonight, okay?

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:27.720
<b>Minami</b>

00:21:30.110 --> 00:21:32.220
We should talk to her.

00:21:32.670 --> 00:21:33.980
I'll tell her.

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:34.820
Wait.

00:21:34.820 --> 00:21:36.900
As the oldest one, I should.

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:38.480
No, I will.

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:40.230
For an important matter
like this, I should—

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:41.330
Stay out of this, Brother.

00:21:41.330 --> 00:21:42.950
But I'm the oldest.
Thanks for the food.

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:43.060
But I'm the oldest.

00:21:43.060 --> 00:21:44.120
Shut up!

00:21:45.290 --> 00:21:48.900
I guess I'll have to clean
.up after them again.

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:24.420
I'd like to call to order the Eighth Meeting
for Making Touma More Ladylike.

00:23:24.420 --> 00:23:26.130
Something tells me that
eighth time's not the charm.

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:28.130
Stay out of this, Akira!

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:31.020
Next time: Simply Put,
It's a Roundabout Confession.

00:23:31.020 --> 00:23:32.320
It's a confession?!
